title: AutoGen maps boolean array items to ArrayRef[Str], rejecting schema-true payloads
updated: 2026-08-27T18:48:15Z
---

lib/IO/K8s/AutoGen.pm:279-282 -- items: { type: boolean } falls into
the default ["Str"]; JSON booleans (JSON::PP::Boolean refs) then fail
ArrayRef[Str], so schema-conforming data is rejected with a type error
that never names the real problem (wrongly generated attribute type).

Repro (measured): flags => [JSON::PP::true, JSON::PP::false] dies with
did not pass type constraint "Maybe[ArrayRef[Str]]".

Fix sketch: return the [Bool] form for boolean items -- the DSL already
has the array-of-bool path with per-element normalization
(is_array_of_bool); only the AutoGen mapping misses it. Mind karr #51
(undef element emission) when touching this area.

Found in the 2026-08-18 core-module review (repro verified).
Lane: io-k8s-worker, then io-k8s-test-writer (t/04_autogen.t).

Fixed: boolean array items map to the [ Bool ] form. Item types are now Type::Tiny objects, not barewords -- ['Bool'] would have been read as a class name (InstanceOf['IO::K8s::Api::Bool']). Tests: t/57_autogen_karr_55_60.t.
